  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile avgpool is best (acc 0.650, F1 0.628), while the only multimodal extension with ResNet50 and concat is slightly weaker (acc 0.632, F1 0.607); image-only ResNet50 is also weak, so the key uncertainty is whether the lack of multimodal gain is due to a weak image encoder. config_036 tests exactly this by replacing ResNet50 with imagenet_vit_l while keeping scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, and concat fixed, isolating image representation. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the best RNA pipeline, directly clarifies whether a stronger image modality can make the model competitive, and avoids changing multiple factors at once."
}

